  "behavior": [
    "Common-sign rational degree-one spans traverse exact source chords. Reversals and nonempty span boundaries remain in order; constant spans collapse. Mixed signs and discontinuities decline.",
    "Conservative BVH query partitioning keeps the exact original rational source chord, outward endpoint bounds and feasible mesh-vertex upper distances. It targets 64 candidates to depth 16 and retains the full path when the largest candidate set does not shrink.",
    "General curve approximation reuses exact de Casteljau subdivision only when the stored native midpoint is exactly halfway. Other midpoints use exact direct restriction at the actual parameter.",
    "Existing tolerance, work, rational-size and output limits remain in force. No sampled acceptance or widened error bound is introduced."
  ],
  "checks": {
    "mesh_index_regressions": 14,
    "mesh_pull_geometry_tests": 15,
    "shared_certificate_regressions": 39,
    "approximation_tests_including_rounded_midpoint": 11,
